            <title>[LU-20630] sanity-lnet test_238: FAIL 'Expect Multi-Rail: false, found False' when the router runs &lt; 2.16</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20630</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-lnet test_238 fails with:&lt;br/&gt;
  Expect 'Multi-Rail: false', found False&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;lnetctl renders the Multi-Rail field from two paths that disagree on case:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Netlink: liblnetconfig_netlink.c:708, NLA_FLAG -&amp;gt; "true"/"false"&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;legacy cYAML: liblnetconfig.c:4204 -&amp;gt; "True"/"False"&lt;br/&gt;
jt_show_peer() (lnetctl.c:6076) falls back to the legacy path on -EOPNOTSUPP, i.e. whenever the&lt;br/&gt;
kernel lacks the LNet genl peer command. That command landed in 8a0fdfa0b2 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-10391" title="LNET: Support IPv6" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-10391"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-10391&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, 2023-08-07),&lt;br/&gt;
so b2_16 and master have it and b2_15 does not.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;test_238 reads the flag from ${ROUTERS&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;0&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;} and compares it exactly against lowercase 'false', so it&lt;br/&gt;
fails whenever the router node runs &amp;lt; 2.16. In the run below the router onyx-159vm113 was running&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre 2.15.8.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity-lnet.sh:3055 parses the same field and compares against 'False' instead, so the file already&lt;br/&gt;
disagrees with itself; that site fails open (it skips wrongly) which is why only 238 is visible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Pre-existing: test_238 was added by bb6237483d (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19827" title="MR Forwarding not working correctly after LU-18444" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19827"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-19827&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, 2025-11-19). It passes in most configs&lt;br/&gt;
because whether a &amp;lt;2.16 node lands in the router slot is a node-allocation lottery.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Suggested fix: compare case-insensitively (${mr,,}) at both sites in lustre/tests/sanity-lnet.sh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/a65cae94-5d3b-4b85-b01e-4643435cdfb4" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/a65cae94-5d3b-4b85-b01e-4643435cdfb4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
